.TH DTSRCLEAN 1 "2026-11-22" "Amiga UNIX add-on" "CDE"
.SH NAME
dtsrclean \- compress and check a DtSearch database
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B dtsrclean
.RB [ \-p\c
.IR N ]
.RB [ \-oy | \-on ]
.RB [ \-v [\c
.IR file ]]
.RB [ \-c\c
.IR N ]
.I database
.I newpath
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B dtsrclean
copies the word index of the DtSearch database
.I database
(its
.I .d99
and
.I .d2x
files) into the directory
.IR newpath ,
leaving out the space that deleted records left unused.
The old files are read only; the new ones replace them when the
administrator moves them into place.
.I database
is the 1 to 8 character database name, found in the current directory or
on
.BR DBFPATH .
A relative
.I newpath
is relative to the current directory.
.TP 12
.BI \-p N
print a progress dot every
.I N
records (default 1000), and a progress line every 50 dots
.TP
.B \-oy
overwrite
.I .d99
and
.I .d2x
files already in
.I newpath
.TP
.B \-on
exit if there are such files
.TP
.BR \-v [\c
.IR file ]
also check every link between the
.I .d99
and
.I .d00
files, repair the
.I .d99
file and correct the record count; with
.IR file ,
write the
.I .d00
records no
.I .d99
entry refers to into
.I file
in the form
.BR dtsrload (1)
reads
.TP
.BI \-c N
exit after more than
.I N
damaged or incomplete links (default 100);
.B \-c0
never exits for them
.SH EXIT STATUS
0 success; 1 warnings; 2 the job did not start; 3 to 49 the job ended
early, the old files are good and the new ones unusable; 50 to 99 a fatal
error that may have damaged the old database too; 100 and above a signal
(the exit status less 100) ended the job, and the new files may be
unusable.
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR dtsrcreate (1),
.BR dtsrdbrec (1),
.BR dtsrdelete (1),
.BR dtsrload (1)
